{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The USB flash drive feels useful for moving files between my laptop and Raspberry Pi setup, which fits my practical accessory purchases.",
    "Portable storage connects with my past memory-card purchases while offering a different use from the cards I already have."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Another HDMI cable or keyboard repeats equipment I already have without addressing a current replacement need.",
    "The speaker wire, tripod and streaming device assume projects I have not shown an immediate interest in pursuing.",
    "The RAM, internal hard drive and Fire-focused memory card require compatibility or upgrade needs I have not established."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My computer accessory purchases seem to have been treated as interest in almost any computer component, even parts that require a specific machine and upgrade plan.",
    "My headphone and HDMI purchases seem to have been stretched into interest in speaker installations and streaming devices, although those serve different needs."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My recent purchases suggest practical setup and maintenance needs, such as wired connectivity, desk organization, cleaning and carrying equipment.",
    "Accessories that complement what I already use are more appealing right now than duplicates or hardware that needs an unconfirmed compatible system."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognize my interest in practical electronics but often miss the specific task, compatibility and existing equipment that determine whether I need an item now."
}"}
